{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1487421-dungeons-dragons-movie-trailer-is-out","id":1487421,"title":"Dungeons & Dragons Movie Trailer is out!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-21T15:44:28-07:00","id":1487421,"title":"Dungeons & Dragons Movie Trailer is out!","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IiMinixSXII\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IiMinixSXII\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IiMinixSXII\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IiMinixSXII </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thought this might be interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have some comments, but gonna let you see it first and make your own opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T17:11:38-07:00","id":1487428,"title":"","content":"This looks better than the last time they tried this... but that's a pretty low bar tbh. CGI looks MUCH better, but it has no excuse not to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T18:03:46-07:00","id":1487430,"title":"","content":"Saw the kerfluffle on how the artist who made the movie poster straight up copy/pasted material from Pathfinder's artwork into the poster. So we're already getting controversies.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FYKOyD5UIAAw3PX?format=jpg&amp;name=900x900\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.redd.it/iz7hfcutvyc91.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Looks like they quickly deleted that poster off twitter and put up a new one its place. Still, that's a big whoopsie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-21-2022, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T02:14:59-07:00","id":1487464,"title":"","content":"The trailer looks good though. Guardians of the Galaxy: D&amp;D edition. Also looks like it'll take place in the Forgotten Realms. That really looks like Gracklstugh, and I'm positive that fat, cubby red dragon is Themberchaud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T04:53:49-07:00","id":1487474,"title":"","content":"My primary reaction is... what's going to be the hook that makes this great instead of just finally being a good D&amp;D movie. The trailer screams, &quot;OK, GoT was a bit deal, the MCU makes this sort of thing work, so... lets just do those things in D&amp;D.&quot; Which sure, seems like it will be a good flick to catch on whatever streaming service it goes to at some point. I want to see something more before I'm going to think about paying extra money to see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T12:48:26-07:00","id":1487501,"title":"","content":"Upon some further rumination:<br /> <br /> I think part of the problem for a D&amp;D movie (and really most RPG adaptations) is that it's a preexisting setting without preexisting characters for us to want to see come to the big screen (though for me at least, that means as much&quot;I don't want to see a Drizzt movie&quot; as much as RPGs tend to lack a core cast).<br /> <br /> Like sure, there's going to be some stuff for Forgotten Realms (that's confirmed by the way) fans to enjoy seeing. Like the core group is &quot;[assume human unless otherwise stated] [Name] [Class].&quot; We're going to need not just how the film is going to interpret a specific take on some established characters, but it's going to have to establish a bunch of new characters in the first place; something that hurt the previous D&amp;D movies beyond other issues with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T14:58:06-07:00","id":1487510,"title":"","content":"It might be worth checking out once and the CGI is way better then previous versions. But I haven't been impressed with adaptaions of my favorite games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T18:00:52-07:00","id":1487527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1487421-dungeons-dragons-movie-trailer-is-out?p=1487501#post1487501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like sure, there's going to be some stuff for Forgotten Realms (that's confirmed by the way) fans to enjoy seeing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it looks like this is intended to be something of a crosscut of the Forgotten Realms, to showcase some of the setting and creatures that exist there. According to the interview some of the locations include Neverwinter and Ten Towns and, I would guess likely Waterdeep will appear at some point (because that's sort of the central city to the setting), along with many of the more iconic monsters and races that populate the world (I noticed Sophia Eleni is credited as a Tabaxi mother and Sophia Liliis is a Tiefling druid). They probably intend for the movie to serve as an &quot;introduction to the Dungeons and Dragons setting&quot; and to help set it apart from the other other fantasy movies that people may be familiar with. This will serve to introduce everything to people new to the franchise, while still offering a lot of neat stuff for long time fans.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing the goal is to present the movie as a bit of a buffet with a lot of different things to encourage people to try out table top gaming or try some of D&amp;D's video games, novels or other materials. Very much so, I feel like the goal is not necessarily to make a &quot;great&quot; movie, but to have this movie be a commercial for the larger franchise. Like they obviously want to the movie to be successful, but I'm feeling like they want to it function as a vehicle for getting new people into the hobby. So they're taking cues from other successful movies and we'll get something that's entertaining and fun with lots of easter eggs and references for long time fans. And if it's successful, maybe they'll make another movie at some point in the future.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I'm not expecting it to be a &quot;great&quot; movie but just a fun movie, especially if you're a D&amp;D fan and familiar with the Forgotten Realms. The usage of &quot;Original Characters&quot; over famous NPCs will also help to set the tone of using the movie as an example for a D&amp;D party and campaign.<br /> <br /> As an aside I'm guessing there will be a post-credits meta-scene that shows all of the actors sitting around a kitchen table, making it clear that the movie was their D&amp;D session. Maybe Chris Pine will be sitting there complaining about some moment that happened in the movie and saying, &quot;If I hadn't rolled a natural one there...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-23-2022, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T08:43:39-07:00","id":1487595,"title":"","content":"Maybe we will see a version of Drizzt or Cyric being mentioned or seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:35:29-07:00","id":1487665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1487421-dungeons-dragons-movie-trailer-is-out?p=1487595#post1487595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we will see a version of Drizzt or Cyric being mentioned or seen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would love to see a big budget movie set in the Underdark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T18:58:23-07:00","id":1487672,"title":"","content":"The problem is that this is why the DCEU has struggled so much more than the MCU. The MCU started with a bunch of movies that focused on individual characters, and a small handful of relevant locations. Then you get to do the Avengers.<br /> <br /> The DC movies jumped from one Superman movie into The Big Three of the DC, to the Justice League. The much better received Wonder Woman and Aquaman movies really should have been done before the team ups started.<br /> <br /> It feels like we're going to get something like that, but squeezed into 2.5 hours. &quot;Oh hey, Themyscira and Amazons! Hey Atlantis and merfolk! Oh hey Star City (and Iris West in the Synder Cut)! It's too much for a single film, so whatever shortcuts happen are going to make the movie less than it could been if handled better.<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of the Drizzt stuff... but a Drizzt movie that can focus on one character and immediate related cast, doesn't need to cut corners between character development, story, action, and world building. Three or four movies like that, and then you have enough audience understanding of your cinematic world to start doing &quot;band of PCs&quot; style movies that don't suffer from having to explain too much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T09:18:57-07:00","id":1487737,"title":"","content":"Again, I think the goal for the movie is to have it serve as something of an example of D&amp;D play, which necessitates having a party of adventurers. You can't do a solo flick and hold that up as an example of what playing a game of Dungeons and Dragons is like because having a party dynamic is a pretty central to the basic concept of Dungeons and Dragons (and indeed, roleplaying in general). Having a solo focused movie would no doubt leave a lot of D&amp;D fans scratching their heads, trying to reconcile that with what a D&amp;D campaign is actually like.<br /> <br /> I think there is room for solo movie stuff in D&amp;D (though to note even with Drizzt his adventuring party and companions play an incredibly important role in his storyline) but for a &quot;this is a very general example of what Dungeons and Dragons is like&quot; movie intended to introduce and represent D&amp;D to non-fans, I feel that a party is pretty much mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T13:11:26-07:00","id":1487770,"title":"","content":"Repeatedly telling me what you think the &quot;goal&quot; is, doesn't do anything to alleviate my concerns based on decades of watching movies where it's a goal that's helpful to making a good movie or not.<br /> <br /> We have places to watch examples of D&amp;D play if we want to see that.<br /> <br /> Adaptations need to <b>adapt</b> and failing to do so diminishes the final product. Skipping over all the stuff that happens in Session Zero/preludes/etc. in RPGs and trying to throw PC analogues into the thick of things without enough context is not going to meet the goal you're proposing effectively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T17:19:33-07:00","id":1487810,"title":"","content":"There have been a lot of movies over the years and quite a few of them have involved a small group of characters who find themselves thrown into the thick of things. In fact, starting off with various solo movies and then slowly pulling those characters together into a movie with one another is a pretty rare and recent phenomenon. Outside of the Marvel movies I can't really think of any other examples of it. It's not like with Star Wars: Episode 4 we first needed a a Han Solo movie, and then a Princess Leia movie, and then a Luke Skywalker movie and then an Obi-wan movie building up to a movie involving all four of those characters.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible to make a movie involving a setting and a group of characters that are unknown to the audience and do it well. Again, I'd point towards, well, the entirety of the history of movies as examples. Will the D&amp;D movie be good? Who knows. But I don't see how the decision to make a movie about a group of adventurers instead of a movie about a single person is somehow a knock against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T20:54:23-07:00","id":1487838,"title":"","content":"How many of those movies are trying to communicate an existing setting, with existing characters, that audiences are supposed to then buy additional media for/engage with in other ways as a primary consideration, while focusing on different characters from those?<br /> <br /> Movie history is full of mediocre films that overly rely on tropes and cliches to replace good character developments.<br /> <br /> Star Wars, if only one movie was ever made, wouldn't be seen as much of a movie. It's only because of the first trilogy we have the cultural impact it has, because ESB and RotJ let it grow beyond being a fairly typical Space Opera with neat special effects.<br /> <br /> Ensemble films are notoriously difficult films. The ones that work tend to skew perceptions because making them work is so hard that when you do, you have a great film on your hands. All of the failures tend to get memory holed. Consider that the Oscars have four main acting awards, not an &quot;ensemble&quot; award. Ensemble films also tend to avoid action films because, again, limitations of the medium especially time. Ensemble films in a drama piece are easier to happen because you don't have big action set pieces to try to work into things.<br /> <br /> As for existing examples? Horror is chock full of them. The Universal and Hammer Horror movies were basically the original &quot;cinematic universes.&quot; There's also plenty of it in non-western media as well. Or look at the Fast and Furious films and their wild success considering how things started.<br /> <br /> What you're not paying attention to is my complaint that they're <b>trying to do too much</b>. Yes, a single party of original characters to make things more like a D&amp;D game can work, but you can't also make it a world tour of Forgotten Realms, and let every character's history and motivations be addressed, and communicate D&amp;D tropes to people that don't know them, and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T04:23:41-07:00","id":1487860,"title":"","content":"I was hoping not to poison the well with my thoughts on the movie as the first poster, so here's some mussings from me. I think that the ensamble cast concept is tricky to execute but a good idea for starting a D&amp;D franchise (and let's face it, that's what Hasbro/Wizards wants here), especially as they seem to be trying for a Guardians of the Galaxy feel - something quite common at tables and in shows like Critical Role. Mind you, the trailer did evoke a certain level of dread for me thinking &quot;wait, what if this trailer is trying to salvage good faith just like the original suicide squad did&quot;.<br /> <br /> In general I feel the movie would do better if it takes itself less seriously and leans into strong protagonists with good banter. Alas, the trailer only showed us that the barbarian and the bard have a good rapport and that the druid is playing the straight (wo)man. I got no idea about who and what the wizard and paladin are supposed to be or if they have any kind of chemistry with the rest, which is I hope just down to the trailer's cut. For that reason the monsters also work, they are slightly cartoony (I do hope the CGI gets one more pass before release, though) rather then hyperrealistic which might vibe well with the tone if it is more of a ensamble action comedy.<br /> <br /> My chief concern comes from the level of stuff we've seen in the trailer. Somehow this group of characters seems to go through the Underdark (Grackstulgh most likely since the fat dragon is the one powering its foundries), Neverwinter and Waterdeep. Add to that that there are Harpers, Council of Waterdeep, Dragons and Wizards of Thay either in Thay or somewhere in the Sword Coast. That's a lot of distance and a lot of story you need to move between those spots and factions. I sincerely hope they don't go too far into exposition mode, because it's really going to bite them in the butt. Mind you, these folks made the Lego Batman and Spiderman:Homecoming so there might have a solid grasp of how to adapt a franchise in an approchable way.<br /> <br /> Another observation is how Wizards is going into trademarks hard - be it displaying mechanics and design acurate dragons, or leaning into the monsters and setting elements they specifically have copyright to.<br /> <br /> At this point I'm happy to say the trailer amused me and I think it could be fun, but if they are masking a much more serious movie, or try leaning into realism it's going to fall apart like a house of cards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1487421-dungeons-dragons-movie-trailer-is-out?p=1487838#post1487838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Star Wars, if only one movie was ever made, wouldn't be seen as much of a movie. It's only because of the first trilogy we have the cultural impact it has, because ESB and RotJ let it grow beyond being a fairly typical Space Opera with neat special effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I generally agree with you on the sentiment about ensamble films as something that has a lot of work to do to actually be good, I'd like to contest this thesis. Way before ESB, Star Wars was a cultural behemoth and spent a ridiculous amount of time in cinemas as well as being a highly successful transmedia property practically out of the door. The first movie was a nuclear explosion as far as recognition, sales and merch went. The later stuff just built into the juggernaut to make it more so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 07-25-2022, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}